WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:21.120
The saved reading index has eleven Week 11 rows. It lists all clinical pathways, BCPEG treatment protocols, endocrine and immune review, heart-failure types, clinical judgment and focused assessment, diagnosis and planning, analyzing cues, pain and respiratory pharmacology, mood disorders and diagnostic reasoning.
学校保存的阅读索引包含第11周十一项阅读：全部临床流程、BCPEG 治疗方案、内分泌与免疫复习、心衰类型、临床判断与重点评估、诊断与计划、线索分析、疼痛与呼吸药理、情绪障碍及诊断推理。

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:35.544
Nancy Caroline’s Canadian 8th edition is the learner-confirmed principal examination text, but it does not replace any of the eleven separate rows. Its selected chapter bridge is clearly labelled as additional study.
Nancy Caroline 加拿大第八版是学员确认的考试主教材，但不能替代上述十一项单独阅读。其选取章节衔接阅读会明确标为补充学习。

00:00:35.544 --> 00:01:01.128
The eleven assigned readers now have source-specific English and Chinese explanations, with the actual files and review extents recorded. Repeated content retains genuine earlier source and meaning checks. This is not merely a collection of candidate summaries. The clinical rounds connect those readings to the patient; they do not claim every linked image, video or assessment has been completed.
十一项指定读本现已提供针对来源的中英文讲解，并记录实际文件与核对范围。重复内容保留真实的既往来源和语义核对，不再只是候选摘要的集合。临床轮次把阅读与患者联系起来，但不声称每个链接图像、视频或考核都已完成。

00:01:01.128 --> 00:01:32.040
The remaining differences are specific. The identified cardiovascular book contains the named heart-failure chapter but not the school table page range. The CPSC sedation table has duplicate score descriptions, and the pharmacology table has an inhaler dose-unit error. The readers explain the available assigned content and these corrections without pretending the locators or products are interchangeable. Current law, provider level and service guidance still govern actual care.
剩余差异是具体的：已识别的心血管教材包含点名的心衰章节，但与学校表格页码不符；CPSC镇静表重复评分描述，药理表则有吸入器剂量单位错误。读本讲解现有指定内容及这些纠正，不假装不同定位或产品可以互换。实际照护仍以现行法律、执业层级和服务指导为准。

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:50.664
The BCEHS and BCPEG reading rows are not one interchangeable source. BCPEG is a saved provincial examination snapshot. Current BCEHS pages are service guidance. Read both when assigned, keep their revision context visible and do not average conflicting instructions.
BCEHS 与 BCPEG 阅读条目并非可以互换的同一来源。BCPEG 是保存的省级考试快照；BCEHS 当前网页是服务指南。两者都要按要求阅读并标清版本，不能把冲突指示取平均。

00:01:50.664 --> 00:02:06.984
For clinical use, check the current pathway and the line for your provider level. The school snapshot can help with examination recall, but a school page, a nursing textbook or a high-stakes exam diagram does not independently authorize an intervention.
临床使用时，应查阅现行流程和自己执业层级对应的条目。学校快照有助于考试复习，但学校页面、护理教材或考试图示都不会自动授权某项干预。

00:02:06.984 --> 00:02:21.840
Do not read only the sentence that contains a familiar term. Read the page heading, surrounding paragraph, figure and provider-level notes. Ask what the author is describing and which setting or profession the statement belongs to.
不要只读含熟悉术语的一句话。应阅读页标题、上下文、图示和执业层级说明。弄清作者描述的情境及该内容属于哪个工作场景或专业。

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:36.096
Close the book and explain the mechanism in your own words. Then connect it to one observation in the Week 11 cases. Keep a note of any exact school edition, linked figure or lab detail that is still missing.
合上教材，用自己的话解释机制，再把它联系到第11周案例中的一个观察。记录仍缺少的确切学校版本、链接图示或实验室细节。

00:02:36.096 --> 00:02:53.544
The two CNS page ranges teach different material. The first eleven pages cover nutritional context, specialized diets and feeding routes; the final five cover clinical judgment. Keeping the page range while teaching only the model would not meet the school reading requirement.
CNS两段页码教授不同材料。前十一页涵盖营养背景、特殊饮食及营养途径；后五页涵盖临床判断。只保留页码却仅教模型，不能满足学校阅读要求。

00:02:53.544 --> 00:03:13.440
Connect the nutrition review to an incomplete medical history. Ask about usual intake and recent change, an existing renal or carbohydrate plan, medicine timing, swallowing difficulty or a feeding device when relevant. These facts can change the questions and safety plan without proving the cause.
应将营养复习联系不完整内科病史。相关时询问平常摄入及近期变化、既有肾病或碳水计划、药物时间、吞咽困难或营养装置。这些事实可改变提问及安全计划，但不证明病因。

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:28.992
The bilingual guide explains each diet and route category in the actual assigned pages. It distinguishes US nutritional teaching from individualized care and leaves the patient’s assessed feeding plan and current service procedure intact.
中英指南解释实际指定页中的各饮食及途径类别，区分美国营养教学与个体化照护，并保留患者已评估喂养计划及当前服务规程。

00:03:28.992 --> 00:03:45.984
Enteral nutrition reaches the gastrointestinal tract through the selected tube. Parenteral nutrition reaches the circulation through a selected venous route. Neither label tells you that an unfamiliar tube or line is correctly positioned or may be used by a PCP student.
肠内营养经所选导管进入胃肠道，肠外营养经所选静脉途径进入循环。任何标签都不能证明陌生导管位置正确，或可由PCP学生使用。

00:03:45.984 --> 00:04:07.944
The assigned page confuses peripheral insertion with peripheral tip location when discussing parenteral nutrition. A PICC is a central line despite its insertion site. Selected NICE guidance also recognizes suitable peripheral venous nutrition in specific short-term circumstances, so not all parenteral nutrition is automatically central.
指定页讨论肠外营养时混淆外周插入与尖端位于外周。PICC虽在外周插入，但仍是中心导管。选取的NICE指导也认可特定短期情境使用合适外周静脉营养，因此并非全部肠外营养都自动属于中心途径。

00:04:07.944 --> 00:04:25.368
For this week, identify the existing device and plan, assess the actual clinical concern and pass accurate information forward. Do not turn textbook maintenance routines into permission to flush, restart a feed or access a line whose use has not been authorized.
本周应识别既有装置及计划、评估真实临床担忧，并准确交接信息。不能把教材维护常规当作冲洗、重启喂养或使用未获准通路的许可。

00:04:25.368 --> 00:04:41.592
The reading set links body mechanisms with bedside observation and protocol use. A hypothesis should explain several cues, fit the timing and survive comparison with alternatives. It remains a hypothesis until the clinical picture supports it.
这组阅读把身体机制与现场观察、流程使用连接起来。一个假设应能解释多条线索、符合时间变化，并经得起与其他可能的比较。在临床表现支持之前，它仍然只是一个假设。

00:04:41.592 --> 00:05:00.840
For the bradycardia case, connect conduction, medication history, renal context and perfusion. For the fall, connect anticoagulant use, possible hidden bleeding, the limb exam and repeated distal checks. Then use the current pathway and say what new finding would alter urgency.
心动过缓案例要联系传导、用药史、肾脏背景及灌注；跌倒案例要联系抗凝药、可能的隐匿出血、肢体检查及重复远端检查。随后使用现行流程，并说明哪些新发现会改变紧急程度。

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:18.528
The actual school-folder copy now resolves the PMHN locator. Printed pages four-eighty through five-oh-eight are physical pages four-ninety-four through five-twenty-two. This is a bounded reading range, not a claim to have covered every page of Chapter Sixteen.
学校文件夹真实版本现已核对PMHN定位。印刷页480至508对应物理页494至522。这是明确的指定阅读范围，不表示涵盖第16章每一页。

00:05:18.528 --> 00:05:38.112
The middle of the assignment covers self-harm and suicide. A course that teaches only depression and bipolar definitions would miss that requirement. The bilingual reading explains assessment, immediate safety and continuity without reproducing the textbook’s cases, answer choices or hospital orders.
指定范围中段涵盖自伤与自杀。若课程只教抑郁及双相定义，就会漏掉这项要求。中英阅读讲解评估、即时安全及照护连续性，不复制教材案例、答案选项或住院医嘱。

00:05:38.112 --> 00:05:53.064
Read the material as a US nursing text adapted to the school’s PCP learning aim. Current BC clinical and legal sources remain separate; a textbook page does not grant a medicine, restraint or disposition authority.
应将本书视为按学校PCP学习目标改编的美国护理教材。当前BC临床及法律来源另行区分；教材页面不授予药物、约束或去向决定权限。

00:05:53.064 --> 00:06:11.784
Low mood alone does not explain an entire presentation. Ask what changed in interest, sleep, appetite, energy, thinking and daily function, how long it lasted and how it differs from usual. A physical complaint may be important even when a mood diagnosis is already recorded.
低心境本身不能解释全部表现。应询问兴趣、睡眠、食欲、精力、思考及日常功能的变化，持续多久，与平常有何不同。即使已有心境诊断，躯体主诉仍可能重要。

00:06:11.784 --> 00:06:32.544
For an activated pattern, ask about increased activity and reduced need for sleep over the relevant period. Mania is not simply being cheerful or talking fast; a longitudinal professional assessment determines the diagnosis. A known psychiatric history does not rule out a new medical or toxicologic problem.
活动增多模式应询问相关时期的活动增加及睡眠需求减少。躁狂不只是愉快或说话快；诊断需要专业纵向评估。已知精神病史不能排除新的医学或毒理问题。

00:06:32.544 --> 00:06:45.192
Use the person’s own account, observed behaviour and attributed collateral together. Record uncertainties and the immediate needs rather than assigning a label to make an incomplete history appear complete.
应结合本人叙述、观察行为及注明来源的旁证。记录不确定性及即时需要，不靠贴标签让不完整病史看似完整。

00:06:45.192 --> 00:07:06.288
The assigned pages introduce structured assessments, but the favourable description of SAD PERSONS needs a visible correction. Selected NICE guidance advises against using scales or global risk categories to predict future suicide or decide treatment or discharge. This is a current safety comparison, not BC law.
指定页介绍结构化评估，但对SAD PERSONS的正面描述需要明确纠正。选取的NICE指导反对用量表或总体风险类别预测未来自杀，或决定治疗及离院。这是当前安全对照，不是BC法律。

00:07:06.288 --> 00:07:25.080
Use calm direct questions about the present concern and listen without judgment. Assess injury, illness and immediate safety alongside the reported thoughts. A denial of a detailed plan is one finding, not permission to stop assessing or leave without a defensible current plan.
应平静直接询问当前担忧，并不带评判地倾听。在了解想法的同时评估损伤、疾病及即时安全。否认详细计划是一项发现，不允许据此停止评估，或在没有合理现行计划时离开。

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:38.808
Communicate what is known, what remains unclear and who is responsible during the next care transition. A useful record shows the patient’s needs and actual actions; it does not replace them with a reassuring score.
沟通已知内容、未明事项及下一照护转移中的责任归属。有用记录应呈现患者需要及真实行动，不用令人放心的分数代替。

00:07:38.808 --> 00:07:56.928
The assigned lithium pages link medicine safety to kidney function, hydration and interacting medicines. A patient with a mood diagnosis and new vomiting, tremor, unsteadiness or confusion needs a medical assessment; do not assume the change is only a mood episode.
指定锂剂页面把药物安全与肾功能、水合及相互作用药物联系起来。已有心境诊断的患者新发呕吐、震颤、不稳或意识混乱，需要医学评估；不能只当成心境发作。

00:07:56.928 --> 00:08:18.792
Do not use the book’s statement that toxicity begins at two-point-zero as a reassuring cutoff. Current NHS Specialist Pharmacy Service guidance notes that toxicity may occur despite an apparently normal blood level. The field task is recognition, appropriate assessment and timely clinical advice, not laboratory exclusion.
不能把教材“中毒始于2.0”当作令人放心的切点。当前NHS专科药学服务指导指出，即使表面正常血药浓度也可中毒。现场任务是识别、适当评估及及时临床建议，不是进行实验室排除。

00:08:18.792 --> 00:08:33.600
Record the actual medicine history and the symptom timeline and follow the local pathway for the patient’s condition. This course does not instruct a student to prescribe, restart or independently adjust long-term psychiatric medicines.
记录真实药物史及症状时间线，并依患者情况遵循本地流程。本课程不指导学生处方、重启或独立调整长期精神科药物。

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:52.296
The actual CPSC range is more specific than the old generic focused-assessment summary. It starts within neurological examination, crosses breathing and circulation, and stops during abdominal examination. Select the relevant findings without delaying the immediate assessment.
真实CPSC范围比原先泛泛的重点评估摘要具体。它从神经检查中段开始，经过呼吸及循环，结束于腹部检查中段。应选择相关发现，但不能延误即时评估。

00:08:52.296 --> 00:09:08.184
In our original parking-lot case, compare the new confusion with the breathing pattern, perfusion and abdominal complaint. One source heading does not make these four separate patients. The question is how the findings change the current priority and next information need.
在原创停车场案例中，应把新发意识混乱与呼吸模式、灌注及腹部主诉联系起来。四个来源标题不代表四名不同患者。要回答的是：这些发现如何改变当前优先项及下一项信息需要。

00:09:08.184 --> 00:09:23.928
The paired reading gives the actual page-specific concepts and keeps the hospital setting and source limitations visible. Use the existing service assessment pathway for actions; do not add a nursing procedure merely because it appears in the assigned text.
中英阅读提供真实逐页概念，并保留医院场景及来源局限。行动使用既有服务评估流程；不能因指定教材出现某护理操作，就把它加进现场计划。

00:09:23.928 --> 00:09:40.824
The source’s sedation example repeats the same two and three descriptions. We checked the rendered page, so this is not just a text-extraction problem. Report the observed response and use the exact approved tool; never repair a score by guessing its missing anchor.
源文镇静示例重复2分及3分描述。已检查渲染页，证实不只是文字提取问题。应报告观察反应并使用确切获准工具；不能猜测缺失锚点来修补评分。

00:09:40.824 --> 00:09:59.520
Its pulse chart calls three normal, while other charts differ. Its capillary-refill wording separates less than three from more than three without defining exactly three. Describe what you observed and identify the source rather than treating bare numbers as interchangeable clinical conclusions.
该书脉搏表将3定义为正常，而其他表可能不同。其毛细血管再充盈将小于3秒与大于3秒区分，却未定义恰好3秒。应描述所见并指出来源，而不是把裸数字当作可互换临床结论。

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:12.552
A new decline in responsiveness or distal perfusion requires reassessment in its own right. A score, an isolated saturation or a completed checkbox does not cancel that clinical change.
新发反应下降或远端灌注恶化，本身就需要复评。分数、孤立氧饱和度或勾选完成，都不能抵消这一临床变化。

00:10:12.552 --> 00:10:29.832
For the injured patient in the foyer, record the distal findings before an authorized splint or movement and repeat them afterwards. Say which side and site were checked and what was limited. Do not write normal when sensation or movement could not be tested.
门厅伤者获准固定或移动前，应记录远端发现，之后重复检查。说明检查的侧别、部位及局限。感觉或运动无法测试时，不能写正常。

00:10:29.832 --> 00:10:46.152
For the breathless patient, report effort, speech, air entry and the measured trend alongside the response to care. A sound label alone is less useful than a clear account of the new abnormality, its distribution and what changed.
对呼吸困难者，应把呼吸努力、言语、进气及实测趋势，与照护后反应一起报告。仅有呼吸音标签，不如清楚描述新异常、分布及变化有用。

00:10:46.152 --> 00:11:01.992
For abdominal or neurological findings, distinguish the patient’s account from your observation and the possible explanation. Hand over the remaining uncertainty rather than converting a limited field examination into a definitive diagnosis.
对腹部或神经发现，应区分本人叙述、亲自观察及可能解释。应交接剩余不确定性，不能把有限现场检查转为确诊。

00:11:01.992 --> 00:11:18.024
The assigned FON chapter teaches how nursing organizes responses, risks and care plans. Understanding it supports clinical reasoning, but it does not require a PCP to chart a nursing taxonomy or independently adopt US nursing interventions.
指定FON章节教授护理如何组织反应、风险及照护计划。理解它支持临床推理，但不要求PCP记录护理分类，也不允许独立采用美国护理干预。

00:11:18.024 --> 00:11:35.136
Tanner separates noticing, interpreting, responding and reflecting. Reflection during care changes the immediate plan; reflection afterwards guides a later attempt. The measurement model offers another view of the reasoning, not a new treatment permission.
Tanner区分注意、解释、响应及反思。照护期间反思改变即时计划，照护后反思指导后续尝试。测量模型提供另一推理视角，不提供新增治疗权限。

00:11:35.136 --> 00:11:54.120
Predict a plausible complication, prevent a modifiable risk, manage the problem that is present and promote the person’s participation and function. In the original two-patient scene, this means tracking both the current breathing concern and the risk created by an unfinished second-patient assessment.
应预测合理并发症、预防可改变风险、管理现存问题，并促进本人参与及功能。原创双患者场景中，这意味着同时追踪当前呼吸担忧，以及第二位患者评估未完成造成的风险。

00:11:54.120 --> 00:12:10.440
The book introduces actual versus potential and acute versus chronic comparisons. They help organize questions but cannot replace the clinical situation. A minor current complaint does not automatically outrank a credible immediate threat to breathing.
教材介绍实际与潜在、急性与慢性比较。它们有助组织问题，却不能替代临床情境。轻微现存主诉不自动优先于可信的即时呼吸威胁。

00:12:10.440 --> 00:12:26.496
Similarly, a familiar symptom in a chronic illness can worsen. Ask about baseline, severity, new findings and the actual trend. Do not use expected as a reason to ignore a change or use acute as a reason to stop thinking.
同样，慢性病中的熟悉症状也可能恶化。应询问基线、严重度、新发现及真实趋势。不能以预期为由忽视变化，也不能以急性为由停止思考。

00:12:26.496 --> 00:12:38.664
State the current priority and the evidence supporting it, then name the finding that would make you revise the plan. This is the connection between the assigned reading and the school’s semi-autonomous scenario block.
应说明当前优先项及支持证据，再指出哪项发现会使计划修订。这就是指定阅读与学校半自主场景模块之间的联系。

00:12:38.664 --> 00:12:56.688
A useful goal describes an observable patient result, not just an action completed. In the foyer case, assigning a partner to check the second patient is a task. Receiving and using the report is evidence that the communication loop happened; the patient’s response still requires assessment.
有用目标描述可观察患者结果，而不只是一项行动完成。门厅案例中，让搭档检查第二人是一项任务；接收并使用报告，是沟通循环发生的证据，但患者反应仍需评估。

00:12:56.688 --> 00:13:13.536
Make the goal realistic for the person’s baseline, available time and resources. Identify who is acting and which dependency remains unresolved. A requested crew or a message left for a service is not automatically an accepted handover.
目标应符合本人基线、可用时间及资源。应明确谁行动、哪项依赖仍未解决。请求支援或给服务留言，不自动构成已接受交接。

00:13:13.536 --> 00:13:25.656
Evaluate the actual result, record what remains incomplete and revise the plan when it does not work. Do not declare success because a checklist was signed or the original action was performed.
应评价实际结果、记录未完成内容，并在无效时修订计划。不能因清单签字或已实施原行动，就宣布成功。

00:13:25.656 --> 00:13:39.432
Ejection fraction divides the amount ejected by the starting ventricular volume. It is not the total amount ejected and is not the cardiac output. The original diagram uses a common volume scale to show the distinction.
射血分数是射出量除以心室起始容积。它不是射出总量，也不是心输出量。原创图用共同容积尺度显示这一区别。

00:13:39.432 --> 00:14:01.128
In Example A, one-hundred-twenty minus forty-eight gives seventy-two millilitres, and seventy-two divided by one-hundred-twenty is sixty percent. In Example B, eighty minus thirty-two gives forty-eight millilitres, and forty-eight divided by eighty is also sixty percent. The equal fractions describe unequal stroke volumes.
示例A中，120减48得到72毫升，72除以120为60%；示例B中，80减32得到48毫升，48除以80也为60%。相同射血比例描述了不同每搏量。

00:14:01.128 --> 00:14:19.128
Preserved fraction does not establish normal filling or exclude a heart-failure syndrome. Conversely, neither of these hypothetical numbers proves that a patient has heart failure. The school reading locator and the actual book chapter are identified separately in the paired guide.
射血比例保留，不能确立充盈正常或排除心衰综合征。反之，这些假设数字也不能证明患者有心衰。中英指南分别标出学校定位及真实教材章节。

00:14:19.128 --> 00:14:36.864
The chapter connects pressure, renal perfusion and myocardial stretch to neural, hormonal and mechanical responses. Some initially support flow, while natriuretic peptides oppose fluid retention. These are mechanisms, not independent field treatment orders.
本章把压力、肾灌注及心肌牵张联系到神经、激素及机械反应。一些反应初期支持血流，利钠肽则对抗液体保留。这些是机制，不是独立现场治疗医嘱。

00:14:36.864 --> 00:14:53.712
Extra filling and increased vascular resistance can eventually increase work and congestion in a failing heart. Volume and pressure loading also favour different simplified remodeling patterns. More wall thickness does not necessarily mean more effective function.
额外充盈及血管阻力增加，最终可能使衰竭心脏负荷及淤血加重。容量及压力负荷也偏向不同简化重构模式。室壁更厚，不一定意味着功能更有效。

00:14:53.712 --> 00:15:09.768
Use this knowledge to explain the new breathlessness, position intolerance or perfusion concern in the original case, without assuming that every symptom comes from the old heart-failure diagnosis. The current patient and authorized pathway determine the action.
应利用这些知识解释原创案例中的新发气促、体位不耐受或灌注担忧，但不能假定每个症状都来自旧心衰诊断。行动由当前患者状况及获准流程决定。

00:15:09.768 --> 00:15:38.304
The main chemical groups are amino-acid derivatives, peptides/proteins and cholesterol-derived steroids. Catecholamines and thyroid hormones are both amines, but have different solubility and receptor behavior. Peptide hormones usually act at surface receptors; steroids and thyroid hormones commonly use intracellular receptors. Transport-protein binding and clearance affect the duration and measured free versus total hormone.
主要化学类为氨基酸衍生物、肽蛋白及胆固醇衍生类固醇。儿茶酚胺和甲状腺激素都属胺，却有不同溶解性和受体行为。肽通常作用表面受体，类固醇及甲状腺激素常用胞内受体。转运蛋白结合及清除影响持续时间，也影响游离与总激素测值。

00:15:38.304 --> 00:16:09.600
Response depends on hormone concentration, receptor number/sensitivity and intracellular state. Upregulation and downregulation alter responsiveness but are not absolute one-direction rules for every disease. Permissive effects enable another signal, synergy amplifies combined effects, and antagonism produces opposing effects, as with many insulin/glucagon actions. Receptor resistance can cause disease even when hormone is present.
反应取决于激素浓度、受体数量敏感性及胞内状态。上调下调改变响应，却不是每种病都绝对单向。允许作用让另一信号发挥，协同放大联合效应，拮抗产生相反效应，如多种胰岛素与胰高血糖素作用。即使激素存在，受体抵抗也可致病。

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:38.496
Anterior-pituitary GH promotes growth partly through IGF-1 and alters fuel use; excess before versus after growth-plate closure produces different patterns. Prolactin is under important inhibitory dopamine control and rises with appropriate lactation stimulation, not only during pregnancy. A single body feature or an isolated hormone value is not sufficient to diagnose a growth or pituitary disorder in the field.
前叶GH部分经IGF-1促生长并改变供能，生长板闭合前后过多的模式不同。泌乳素受重要的多巴胺抑制控制，可随适当哺乳刺激上升，不只孕期才升。单一外貌或一个激素值不足以现场诊断生长或垂体病。

00:16:38.496 --> 00:17:06.432
The hypothalamus links neural and endocrine control to the pituitary through its stalk. Posterior pituitary is neural tissue that stores/releases hypothalamic hormones; anterior pituitary is glandular tissue receiving releasing/inhibiting signals through portal vessels. Calling the pituitary the master gland does not mean it independently controls every hormone or that the posterior lobe synthesizes ADH.
下丘脑经垂体柄连接神经和内分泌控制。后叶是储放下丘脑激素的神经组织，前叶是腺组织，经门脉收释放抑制信号。称垂体为主腺，不表示其独立控制所有激素，也不表示后叶合成ADH。

00:17:06.432 --> 00:17:33.864
Adrenal cortex has glomerulosa, fasciculata and reticularis zones, associated mainly with mineralocorticoids, glucocorticoids and adrenal androgens respectively. The inner medulla contains chromaffin cells and releases catecholamines after sympathetic stimulation. Cortex and medulla share an organ but have different developmental origins, signals and products; cortisol is not epinephrine.
肾上腺皮质有球状、束状及网状带，分别主要关联盐皮质、糖皮质及肾上腺雄激素；内髓质含嗜铬细胞，受交感刺激放儿茶酚胺。皮髓同一器官却有不同发育来源、信号及产物，皮质醇不等于肾上腺素。

00:17:33.864 --> 00:18:04.344
Insulin promotes GLUT4-mediated uptake in muscle/adipose tissue, supports glycogen, fat and protein storage and reduces hepatic glucose output. It does not open the glucose-entry gate in every cell: usual brain and red-cell uptake is largely insulin independent. Insulin deficiency also permits lipolysis and ketone production, so replacing fluid or lowering a displayed glucose does not alone prove ketoacidosis has resolved.
胰岛素促肌及脂肪GLUT4摄糖，支持糖原、脂肪和蛋白储存，并减肝糖输出。它不负责每个细胞的入糖门，通常脑及红细胞摄糖大多不依赖胰岛素。缺胰岛素也允许脂解产酮，因此补液或显示糖降低不能单独证明酮酸中毒已解。

00:18:04.344 --> 00:18:29.448
The right lymphatic duct usually drains the right upper quadrant: right head/neck, upper limb and thorax. The thoracic duct drains most remaining regions, including both lower limbs, and returns at the left venous angle. The right duct does not drain the entire right half of the body. These routes explain anatomy without identifying an edema cause from side alone.
右淋巴导管通常引流右上象限，即右头颈、上肢及胸。胸导管引流大部分其余区域，包括双下肢，并回到左静脉角。右导管不是引流整个右半身。路径用于解剖，不能只凭哪边肿就认病因。

00:18:29.448 --> 00:18:58.440
Lymph enters a node through afferent vessels, passes through sinuses and leaves through efferent vessels. Nodes filter lymph and provide sites for antigen presentation and lymphocyte activation. Follicles/germinal centers are associated with B-cell responses; other regions support T-cell interactions. A tender or enlarged node suggests a process needing context, not automatic proof of one infection or malignancy.
淋巴经输入管入结，穿淋巴窦，再经输出管离开。结滤淋巴并提供抗原呈递及淋巴激活场所。滤泡及生发中心关联B细胞反应，其他区支持T细胞互动。压痛或肿结提示需结合背景的过程，不能自动证明一种感染或肿瘤。

00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:29.304
Blood immune cells arise from hematopoietic precursors. Neutrophils and macrophages are important phagocytes; monocytes circulate and can contribute tissue populations. Dendritic cells are important antigen presenters. B cells can form antibody-secreting plasma cells, T cells coordinate or kill selected targets, and NK lymphocytes contribute innate cytotoxicity. Not every lymphocyte is adaptive and not every T cell secretes antibody.
血免疫细胞来自造血前体。中性粒与巨噬是重要吞噬细胞，单核在血循环并可贡献组织群；树突细胞是重要呈递者。B可成分泌抗体的浆细胞，T协调或杀特定靶，NK淋巴参与先天杀伤。不是每淋巴都属适应性，也不是T细胞分泌抗体。

00:19:29.304 --> 00:19:58.992
Innate recognition uses pattern-recognition systems for microbial patterns and damaged-cell signals. Recognition can trigger phagocytosis, mediator release and cellular recruitment; it is not antigen-specific clonal memory in the usual B/T-cell sense. Phagocytosis encloses material in a phagosome that can fuse with lysosomal machinery. Some organisms evade killing, so engulfment does not guarantee elimination.
先天识别通过模式识别系统认微生物模式及损伤细胞信号，可引吞噬、介质释放及招募，不等于通常B或T细胞意义的抗原特异克隆记忆。吞噬把物包入吞噬体，随后可与溶酶体系统融合。有些病原逃杀，吞入不保证清除。

00:19:58.992 --> 00:20:26.640
Cytokines coordinate cell behavior, and chemokines are a cytokine group that guides migration. Interferons can promote antiviral states in neighboring cells rather than directly acting as antibodies. Acute-phase proteins such as CRP participate in responses but a raised CRP does not identify the organism or diagnose sepsis alone. Chemotaxis means directed movement along chemical signals.
细胞因子协调细胞行为，趋化因子是引导迁移的一类细胞因子。干扰素可使邻细胞进入抗病毒状态，不是直接充当抗体。CRP等急性期蛋白参与反应，但CRP高不能认病原或单独诊脓毒。趋化指沿化学信号定向移动。

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:54.672
Printed912 pairs10 to the eleventh power with “100trillion,” which is arithmetically inconsistent; the comparison copy’s10 to the twelfth still does not equal100trillion. Do not create a new exact repertoire estimate from this typo. Learn combinatorial receptor diversity, clonal selection and memory, and remember that antigen exposure does not guarantee lifelong protection or symptom-free reinfection.
印刷912页把10的11次方与“100万亿”并列，算术不一致；比较本10的12次方也不等于100万亿。不能从这个错误另创精确受体数量。应学组合性受体多样性、克隆选择及记忆，也应记得抗原接触不保证终身保护或再感染无症状。

00:20:54.672 --> 00:21:28.776
Printed933 Table21.7 actually reverses the thyroid-antibody actions: it labels Graves as receptor blockade and Hashimoto as receptor stimulation. Do not memorize those cells. NIDDK explains Graves through thyroid-stimulating antibodies and Hashimoto through immune-mediated thyroid injury commonly causing reduced hormone output. Hashimoto is not adequately defined as universal TSH-receptor blockade, and a disease name alone does not establish this patient’s current hormone state.
印刷933页表21.7确实把甲状腺抗体作用写反：Graves标为阻断受体，Hashimoto标为刺激受体。不能背这些格子。NIDDK以甲状腺刺激性抗体解释Graves，以免疫性甲状腺损伤、常致激素减少解释Hashimoto。把桥本统一定义成TSH受体阻断也不充分，病名本身不能确定本人当前激素状态。

00:21:28.776 --> 00:21:59.592
Thyroid follicles take up iodide, incorporate iodine into thyroglobulin-associated tyrosines and form T3/T4, storing precursor in colloid before release. T4 has four iodines and T3 three; tissues convert some T4 to the more active T3. TRH/TSH and thyroid-hormone feedback regulate the axis. Transport-protein-bound hormone and free hormone are not interchangeable measurements.
甲状腺滤泡摄碘，把碘加到甲状腺球蛋白相关酪氨酸，形成T3及T4，前体先存胶质再释放。T4四个碘，T3三个，组织把部分T4转成较活跃T3。TRH、TSH及甲状腺激素反馈调轴。蛋白结合激素与游离激素测量不能互换。

00:21:59.592 --> 00:22:41.640
Chapter17 Figure17.19’s70-110mg/dL band is an illustration in this school copy, not the current BCEHS hypoglycemia intervention gate or a universal diagnostic reference range. Do not average it with the comparison copy’s70-100. Explain insulin/glucagon feedback, then interpret a measured glucose with units, symptoms, timing and the current pathway. The accompanying statement that brain/liver/kidney cells lack insulin receptors is not a sound general rule; insulin-independent uptake is not the same as absence of insulin signaling.
第17章图17.19的70至110mg/dL区间是该学校副本的示意，不是现行BCEHS低血糖干预门槛，也不是通用诊断参考值。不能与比较本70至100取平均。应解释胰岛素与胰高血糖素反馈，再结合单位、症状、时间及现行流程理解实测糖。旁文称脑肝肾细胞没有胰岛素受体也不是可靠通则；摄糖不依赖胰岛素，不等于不存在胰岛素信号。

00:22:41.640 --> 00:23:15.600
The assigned endocrine glossary endpoint includes acromegaly, cortex/medulla, ACTH, aldosterone, alpha/beta/delta cells, ANP, calcitonin, cAMP/DAG, EPO, FSH and G protein. Retrieve each as source, stimulus and effect, rather than equating a definition with treatment. Cortisol supports hepatic glucose availability through several metabolic effects; it should not be reduced to the glossary’s glycogen-catabolism wording.
指定内分泌术语终点包括肢端肥大、皮质髓质、ACTH、醛固酮、α／β／δ细胞、ANP、降钙素、cAMP／DAG、EPO、FSH及G蛋白。应以来源、刺激及效应回忆每项，而非把定义当治疗。皮质醇经多种代谢作用支持肝糖可用，不能缩成术语表所谓糖原分解。

00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:47.928
Week11 original integration: a person with diabetes and a transplant becomes confused and breathless but has no fever. Link glucose fuel balance, fluid loss, immunosuppression and infection risk without assuming one diagnosis. Obtain actual glucose and repeated respiratory/perfusion findings, clarify medicines and recent changes, and act on present threats. Neither an absent fever nor correction of one measured value proves the remaining illness has resolved.
第11周原创整合：有糖尿病及移植史者意识混乱、气促却无发热。应联系葡萄糖供能、液体丢失、免疫抑制及感染风险，不先认定单一诊断。获取真实血糖，重复呼吸灌注发现，澄清用药及近期变化，并处理当前威胁。没有发热，或纠正一个实测值，都不证明其余疾病已经解决。

00:23:47.928 --> 00:24:15.264
Nociceptive pain comes from tissue-related noxious stimulation: somatic pain involves structures such as skin, muscle and bone, while visceral pain arises from internal organs and may be diffuse or referred. Neuropathic pain involves a lesion or disease of the somatosensory system and may be burning, shooting or tingling. Descriptors suggest mechanisms but do not establish a diagnosis alone.
伤害感受性痛来自组织相关有害刺激：躯体痛涉及皮肤、肌及骨等，内脏痛来自内脏，可弥散或牵涉到别处。神经病理性痛涉及躯体感觉系统损伤或疾病，可灼烧、放射或刺麻。描述可提示机制，但不能单独确立诊断。

00:24:15.264 --> 00:24:43.488
The five-step model is transduction, conduction, transmission, modulation and perception. A noxious stimulus activates a nociceptor; electrical activity travels through peripheral pathways and relays toward the brain. Spinal and descending systems can amplify or inhibit signaling, and conscious experience integrates those signals with context. A protective withdrawal reflex need not wait for conscious perception.
五步模型为换能、传导、传递、调制及感知。有害刺激激活伤害感受器；电活动沿周围通路及中继向脑传递。脊髓与下行系统可放大或抑制信号，有意识体验再把信号与背景整合。保护性回缩反射不必等待意识感知才发生。

00:24:43.488 --> 00:25:08.496
Pain threshold is the point at which a stimulus becomes painful, not the maximum pain a person can tolerate. Expectations, prior experience, support and physiology affect the experience and expression of pain. Use an appropriate self-report or observational tool, record function and reassess with a comparable method; a score alone is not a judgment of credibility.
痛阈是刺激开始被感为痛的点，不是本人能忍受的最大痛。预期、既往体验、支持及生理会影响疼痛体验与表达。应选适当自评或观察工具，记录功能，并以可比较方式复评；单一评分不能用来判断可信度。

00:25:08.496 --> 00:25:34.080
Acetaminophen is analgesic and antipyretic, with little clinically useful peripheral anti-inflammatory action. Its analgesic mechanism is not completely settled. Ask about every combination cold, sleep and prescription product, total amount and timing, liver disease and alcohol exposure. An apparently ordinary product can contribute to serious cumulative toxicity.
对乙酰氨基酚可镇痛退热，但临床有用的外周抗炎作用很小，其镇痛机制尚未完全明确。应问所有复方感冒、助眠及处方产品、总量与时间、肝病及酒精接触。看似普通的产品也可能促成严重累计毒性。

00:25:34.080 --> 00:26:01.680
Aspirin, ibuprofen and naproxen are NSAIDs. COX inhibition explains analgesic, antipyretic and anti-inflammatory effects, but also GI injury/bleeding and impaired renal perfusion in susceptible people. Dehydration, kidney disease, ulcer/bleeding history, anticoagulants and other NSAIDs change risk; taking a drug with food does not eliminate ulcer or bleeding risk.
阿司匹林、布洛芬及萘普生属于NSAIDs。抑制COX可解释镇痛、退热及抗炎，也可造成易感者胃肠损伤出血及肾灌注受损。脱水、肾病、溃疡出血史、抗凝药及其他NSAIDs会改变风险；随餐服用不能消除溃疡或出血风险。

00:26:01.680 --> 00:26:29.640
Aspirin irreversibly inhibits platelet COX, so its antiplatelet effect lasts beyond its presence in plasma. An analgesic choice is not interchangeable with the separate suspected-ACS aspirin pathway. Ask about bleeding, aspirin-sensitive asthma, hypersensitivity and other medicines; pediatric viral-illness/Reye syndrome warnings also prevent casually transferring adult pain advice to children.
阿司匹林不可逆抑制血小板COX，因此抗血小板作用可超出其在血浆中的存在时间。镇痛用药选择不能与疑似ACS的独立阿司匹林流程混用。应问出血、阿司匹林敏感性哮喘、过敏及其他用药；儿童病毒病与Reye综合征警示也意味着不能随意把成人止痛建议搬给儿童。

00:26:29.640 --> 00:26:59.760
The book places tramadol under nonopioid analgesics, although it has opioid-receptor activity. Teach it as an opioid analgesic with additional norepinephrine/serotonin effects, not as a harmless nonopioid or a guarantee of partial-agonist safety. Sedative combinations, respiratory depression, seizures and serotonergic interactions matter. Neuropathic-pain adjuncts such as duloxetine, pregabalin and local anesthetics have different targets and risks.
教材把曲马多放在非阿片镇痛药下，尽管它有阿片受体作用。应把它作为兼有去甲肾上腺素及血清素作用的阿片镇痛药讲解，不能当无害非阿片药，也不能保证所谓部分激动剂安全。镇静药联用、呼吸抑制、癫痫及血清素相关相互作用都重要。度洛西汀、普瑞巴林及局麻药等神经病理性痛辅助药有不同靶点及风险。

00:26:59.760 --> 00:27:31.368
Opioid agonists activate receptors involved in pain modulation, including mu receptors; analgesia and sedation/respiratory depression can occur through related receptor actions. Morphine is a classic reference agent. Fentanyl is synthetic, hydromorphone and oxycodone are semisynthetic, and heroin is semisynthetic rather than a naturally occurring poppy constituent. Similar class membership does not make dose, potency, route or duration interchangeable.
阿片激动剂激活参与痛调制的受体，包括μ受体；镇痛与镇静、呼吸抑制可来自相关受体作用。吗啡是经典参照药。芬太尼是合成药，氢吗啡酮与羟考酮是半合成药，海洛因也是半合成药，而非罂粟天然成分。属于同类不表示剂量、效价、途径或时效可以互换。

00:27:31.368 --> 00:28:01.608
Codeine depends substantially on CYP2D6 conversion to morphine; genetic variation and interacting drugs can make effect less predictable. Meperidine has a neurotoxic metabolite of concern, especially with impaired clearance. Methadone can have prolonged and variable effects. Fentanyl patches and extended-release oral opioids are not rapid rescue substitutes; do not crush modified-release formulations or improvise conversions.
可待因较依赖CYP2D6转为吗啡，遗传差异及相互作用药会使效果较难预测。哌替啶有需警惕的神经毒性代谢物，清除受损时尤其重要。美沙酮作用可延长且变化。芬太尼贴剂与口服缓释阿片药不是快速救援替代品；不能碾碎控缓释剂型或临时自创换算。

00:28:01.608 --> 00:28:30.912
Nausea, constipation, urinary retention, sedation and hypotension can accompany opioid treatment. Slow or shallow breathing and reduced responsiveness demand immediate airway/breathing assessment, not just another pain score. Alcohol, benzodiazepines and other sedatives increase risk. A previous high tolerated dose does not establish safety after an interruption or in a new acute illness.
阿片治疗可伴恶心、便秘、尿潴留、镇静及低血压。呼吸慢浅、反应下降，需要立即评估气道与呼吸，而不只是再测疼痛评分。酒精、苯二氮䓬类及其他镇静药会增风险。既往能耐受高剂量，不证明停药一段时间或新急病中仍安全。

00:28:30.912 --> 00:28:56.496
Clarify an allergy history: itching/flushing associated with histamine release is not automatically the same as anaphylaxis, but reported airway swelling or a severe reaction cannot be dismissed. The book’s different-structure fentanyl statement is not a guarantee of allergy safety. Document the actual reaction and follow the authorized drug pathway and consultation requirements.
应澄清过敏史：组胺释放有关的瘙痒潮红，不自动等同严重过敏，但不能忽略报告的气道肿胀或严重反应。教材所说芬太尼结构不同，并不保证过敏安全。应记录真实反应，遵循获准用药流程及咨询要求。

00:28:56.496 --> 00:29:26.016
Tolerance is reduced effect after repeated exposure; physical dependence means adaptation that can produce withdrawal when exposure falls. Opioid use disorder involves a problematic pattern with impairment or distress, not merely taking a prescribed opioid or having tolerance/withdrawal under appropriate medical supervision. Use nonjudgmental questions about amount, source, timing and co-use rather than diagnosing addiction from a pain request.
耐受是重复接触后效果降低；躯体依赖是适应后、接触下降可出现戒断。阿片使用障碍涉及造成损害或痛苦的问题性使用模式，不是仅因服处方阿片，或适当医疗监督下有耐受及戒断就成立。应不带评判询问用量、来源、时间及联用，不能因提出止痛要求便诊断成瘾。

00:29:26.016 --> 00:30:01.320
Naloxone competitively antagonizes opioid effects. For a patient with inadequate breathing, support airway and ventilation while following the current opioid-poisoning pathway; the clinical endpoint is improved spontaneous ventilation, not forcing complete wakefulness. Recurrent depression is possible because the opioid can outlast reversal. The book’s20-30minute statement and BCEHS monograph’s30-45minute IM/IV description are not a universal timer or discharge rule.
纳洛酮竞争性拮抗阿片作用。患者呼吸不足时，应支持气道通气，同时遵循现行阿片中毒流程；临床终点是自主通气改善，不是强迫完全清醒。阿片药可能比拮抗作用更久，因此抑制可复发。教材20至30分钟与BCEHS专论IM／IV的30至45分钟描述，都不是通用计时器或出院规则。

00:30:01.320 --> 00:30:30.912
Naloxone can precipitate withdrawal and other adverse responses; the source phrase “only major adverse effect” is too absolute. Naltrexone is a longer-term antagonist treatment, not the same emergency reversal product. Nalbuphine is a mixed agonist/antagonist analgesic, not an interchangeable rescue antidote. Know the distinctions without importing the book’s hospital schedules or creating a new PCP drug entitlement.
纳洛酮可诱发戒断及其他不良反应，源文“唯一主要不良反应”过于绝对。纳曲酮是较长期拮抗剂治疗，不等同急救逆转产品。纳布啡是混合激动拮抗镇痛药，不是可互换的急救解毒药。应掌握区别，而非照搬教材医院给药时间表或新增PCP用药权限。

00:30:30.912 --> 00:31:01.368
Original retrieval: a patient with a painful wrist has taken a combination cold remedy and an unknown pain tablet, then becomes difficult to keep awake. First assess breathing, responsiveness and perfusion; obtain products, amounts, times and co-ingestants. Less reported pain with falling alertness is not successful analgesia. Reassess both comfort/function and safety, and explain the medication uncertainty in handover.
原创回忆练习：腕痛患者服了复方感冒药及不明止痛片，随后难以保持清醒。先评估呼吸、反应及灌注，再核对产品、用量、时间与联用物。疼痛报告变少、清醒度下降，不等于镇痛成功。舒适功能与安全都要复评，并在交接说明用药未知。

00:31:01.368 --> 00:31:30.624
Obstruction limits airflow through narrowed airways; restriction limits expansion or available lung volume. Asthma includes variable narrowing and inflammation. COPD includes chronic airway and alveolar abnormalities; emphysema involves destruction of alveolar walls and loss of elastic recoil, not just the book’s generic airway-damage description. A bronchodilator does not reverse every cause of breathlessness.
阻塞使空气难以通过狭窄气道，限制性问题则限制扩张或可用肺容积。哮喘包括可变狭窄及炎症。COPD涉及慢性气道及肺泡异常；肺气肿涉及肺泡壁破坏与弹性回缩丢失，不只是教材笼统的气道损伤。支气管扩张药不能逆转所有气促原因。

00:31:30.624 --> 00:31:56.568
Beta2 agonists relax bronchial smooth muscle. Albuterol is the US name for salbutamol; levalbuterol is another short-acting agent. Salmeterol is long acting and is not a substitute for immediate rescue in an acute attack. Do not generalize that all beta stimulation relaxes all tissues: cardiac beta effects differ, and beta2 selectivity is not absolute.
β2激动剂松弛支气管平滑肌。Albuterol是salbutamol的美国名称，左旋沙丁胺醇是另一短效药。沙美特罗为长效药，不能代替急性发作的即时救援。不能泛化成所有β刺激都使所有组织松弛：心脏β效应不同，β2选择性也不是绝对。

00:31:56.568 --> 00:32:23.688
Check tremor, palpitations, heart rate/rhythm, breathing and the actual response after a beta agonist. A beta blocker or other sympathomimetic can change the response. Reduced wheeze alone is not enough: air entry, speech, effort, fatigue, mentation and oxygenation can reveal continuing or worsening obstruction, including a very quiet chest with poor airflow.
β激动剂后应检查震颤、心悸、心率节律、呼吸及真实反应。β阻滞剂或其他拟交感药可改变反应。喘鸣减少本身不够：进气、说话、呼吸功、疲劳、意识及氧合，可显示持续或恶化的阻塞，包括气流极差时很安静的胸部。

00:32:23.688 --> 00:32:59.928
A source-table safety discrepancy is visible: printed691/692 describes albuterol inhalations as2.5mg per inhalation. Do not use that statement to dose an MDI or convert a nebulizer solution into puffs. The current BCEHS monograph lists a100mcg/spray MDI separately from2.5mg/mL nebules. Verify product, concentration, route, device and the current age/weight/provider-specific instruction before calculating.
源表安全差异必须明示：印刷691及692页把albuterol每次吸入写为2.5毫克。不能据此给MDI定量，也不能把雾化液换算成喷数。现行BCEHS专论把每喷100微克MDI与2.5毫克／毫升雾化液分列。计算前必须核对产品、浓度、途径、装置及现行年龄体重与执业层级指示。

00:32:59.928 --> 00:33:29.040
An inhaler is a drug-device combination. A metered-dose aerosol, dry-powder device and nebulizer require different preparation and inhalation technique. Do not apply the book’s generic four-spray priming, fifteen-second interval or water-cleaning advice to every device. Check the actual instructions, use the appropriate spacer when indicated, assess technique and use teach-back; powder capsules intended for inhalation are not swallowed.
吸入器是药物与装置的组合。定量气雾、干粉及雾化器需要不同准备与吸入技术。不能把教材统一四喷预充、间隔15秒或水洗建议用在所有装置。应核对真实说明、适用时用合适储雾罐、评估技术并请本人复述示范；供吸入的粉末胶囊不能吞服。

00:33:29.040 --> 00:33:57.096
Ephedrine and epinephrine have broader adrenergic effects than a selective inhaled beta2 agonist. Epinephrine’s alpha effects support vasoconstriction and its beta effects include cardiac stimulation and bronchodilation. The textbook’s oral/inhaled/IV/SC/IM list is not permission to interchange routes or use a consumer inhaler instead of the authorized anaphylaxis pathway.
麻黄碱与肾上腺素的肾上腺素能作用，比选择性吸入β2药更广。肾上腺素α效应支持血管收缩，β效应包括心脏刺激及支气管扩张。教材口服、吸入、IV、SC及IM清单，不授权混换途径，也不能拿消费者吸入器代替获准严重过敏流程。

00:33:57.096 --> 00:34:29.832
Ipratropium blocks muscarinic acetylcholine effects on bronchial smooth muscle; tiotropium provides longer maintenance bronchodilation. For the current BCEHS severe-bronchospasm pathway, ipratropium is an adjunct with salbutamol, not acute monotherapy; its repeat instructions are not copied from the textbook. Dry mouth, blurred vision, urinary-retention risk and paradoxical worsening merit attention. Avoid aerosol exposure to the eyes, especially with narrow-angle glaucoma.
异丙托溴铵阻断支气管平滑肌的毒蕈碱型乙酰胆碱效应，噻托溴铵提供较长维持扩张作用。现行BCEHS严重支气管痉挛中，异丙托溴铵与沙丁胺醇辅助联用，不作急性单药治疗；重复指示不能从教材照搬。口干、视物模糊、尿潴留风险及反常恶化均需注意，应避免气雾入眼，窄角型青光眼尤其重要。

00:34:29.832 --> 00:35:01.920
Corticosteroids act through glucocorticoid receptors and altered inflammatory signaling, including gene regulation; “stabilizing lysosomes” is not a complete mechanism. Beclomethasone, fluticasone and budesonide are inhaled examples, while prednisone and methylprednisolone illustrate systemic treatment. Anti-inflammatory benefit is not instantaneous smooth-muscle relaxation, and an inhaled steroid alone is not the rescue bronchodilator for acute severe obstruction.
糖皮质激素通过糖皮质激素受体及炎症信号变化起效，包括基因调节；“稳定溶酶体”不是完整机制。倍氯米松、氟替卡松及布地奈德是吸入例，泼尼松及甲泼尼龙说明全身治疗。抗炎获益不是即时平滑肌松弛，单独吸入激素不是急性严重阻塞的救援扩张药。

00:35:01.920 --> 00:35:36.408
Inhaled steroids can cause local candidiasis and dysphonia; appropriate mouth rinsing and device technique reduce local problems. Systemic exposure can affect glucose, mood, infection risk, blood pressure and other functions. HPA suppression and stopping/tapering decisions depend on exposure and clinical context: do not tell every short-course patient they must taper or that inhaled and systemic risks are identical. Suspected adrenal illness needs assessment, not a self-designed taper.
吸入激素可致局部念珠菌病及发声障碍，适当漱口与装置技术可减局部问题。全身接触可影响血糖、情绪、感染风险、血压等。HPA抑制及停药减量取决于接触与临床背景，不能告诉每位短疗程患者必须递减，也不能把吸入与全身风险等同。怀疑肾上腺相关急病需要评估，而非自创减量方案。

00:35:36.408 --> 00:36:12.216
Theophylline and aminophylline are xanthines with bronchodilator effects and a narrow therapeutic margin. The source’s10-20mcg/mL range is a textbook reference, not a PCP titration target. Vomiting, agitation, tremor, confusion, tachyarrhythmia or seizures can indicate toxicity; interactions and altered clearance matter. Obtain the formulation, last dose, recent illness and medication changes, and do not treat this as an invitation to initiate an infusion.
茶碱与氨茶碱是有扩张作用、治疗窗窄的黄嘌呤药。源文10至20微克／毫升是教材参照，不是PCP滴定目标。呕吐、激越、震颤、混乱、快速心律失常或癫痫可提示毒性，相互作用及清除变化很重要。应获取剂型、末次剂量、近期疾病与用药变化，不能据此自行开始输注。

00:36:12.216 --> 00:36:41.136
Leukotrienes contribute to bronchoconstriction, mucus and inflammation. Montelukast and zafirlukast block leukotriene receptors; zileuton inhibits leukotriene synthesis. These are not one identical mechanism or acute rescue substitutes. Oral montelukast is not an inhaled dry powder. Hepatic risk and interactions differ between products, so a shared class label does not replace a product-specific history.
白三烯参与支气管收缩、黏液及炎症。孟鲁司特与扎鲁司特阻断白三烯受体，齐留通抑制合成；机制并非完全相同，也不是急性救援替代品。口服孟鲁司特不是吸入干粉。不同产品肝风险及相互作用不同，不能以同类标签代替具体产品病史。

00:36:41.136 --> 00:37:08.016
Cromolyn stabilizes mast cells and reduces mediator release; its role is prevention rather than immediate bronchodilation. It is not naloxone, an antihistamine or a rescue replacement for epinephrine in anaphylaxis. Cough or worsening wheeze after an inhaled product still requires reassessment. Histamine is one mediator, not the entire explanation of every allergic response.
色甘酸稳定肥大细胞、减少介质释放，其作用在预防而非即时扩张。它不是纳洛酮、抗组胺药，也不能在严重过敏中代替肾上腺素救援。吸入产品后咳嗽或喘鸣恶化仍需复评。组胺只是一种介质，不能解释所有过敏反应。

00:37:08.016 --> 00:37:38.880
Montelukast has a serious neuropsychiatric warning, including behavior/mood changes and suicidal thoughts or actions, with or without prior psychiatric illness. The source’s blanket “do not stop” teaching must not override the regulator warning to stop montelukast and contact a clinician immediately for new neuropsychiatric symptoms. Assess immediate safety and report the timing; do not assume a new mental-health presentation is unrelated to medicines.
孟鲁司特有严重神经精神警示，包括行为情绪变化及自杀想法或行为，有无精神病史均可发生。源文统一“不要停药”不能覆盖监管机构对新神经精神症状应停孟鲁司特并立即联系临床人员的警示。应评估即时安全并报告时间关系，不能假设新精神表现与药物无关。

00:37:38.880 --> 00:38:11.976
Original retrieval: a breathless patient points to a daily tiotropium device and says, “I already used my rescue.” Identify the actual product and rescue plan, assess speech/effort/air entry/mentation and look for deterioration. Explain why maintenance bronchodilation and anti-inflammatory control differ from acute rescue. After authorized care, compare the whole respiratory picture with baseline rather than counting puffs as proof of improvement.
原创回忆练习：气促患者指着每日噻托溴铵装置，说“我已经用了急救药”。应识别真实产品与救援计划，评估说话、呼吸功、进气及意识，寻找恶化。解释维持扩张与抗炎控制为何不同于急性救援。获准照护后，要与基线比较整体呼吸状况，不能把喷数当作改善证据。

00:38:11.976 --> 00:38:41.256
Page38 starts IV therapy with a reason: access for an indicated medicine or appropriate fluid replacement. Then maintain asepsis while inspecting the catheter, solution and set, priming tubing, selecting/preparing a site, establishing access, connecting, controlling flow and securing. An open vein does not itself prove a fluid indication, and successful insertion does not finish patient or site monitoring.
第38页先说明静脉治疗理由：为有适应症药物或适当补液建立通路。随后在无菌原则下检查导管、液体与输液器、排气充管、选点备皮、建立通路、连接、控制流速并固定。静脉已通本身不证明需补液，穿刺成功也不等于患者与穿刺点监测结束。

00:38:41.256 --> 00:39:15.816
Page39’s correct dimensional relationship is volume in millilitres times the tubing drop factor in drops per millilitre, divided by minutes. Its worked examples incorrectly label the factor as drops per minute, and one solution description combines5% with D10W; do not copy either error into a label or calculation. Original arithmetic:90mL over45minutes through a10drops/mL set gives20drops/minute. This is arithmetic, not a fluid prescription.
第39页正确量纲关系是：毫升体积乘每毫升滴数的输液器滴系数，再除分钟。其算例把滴系数误标成每分钟滴数，另一个液体描述把5%与D10W并列；不能把两项错误抄进标签或计算。原创算术：90毫升用45分钟、输液器10滴／毫升，得到20滴／分钟。这是算术，不是补液处方。

00:39:15.816 --> 00:39:45.864
The same page describes an approximate75mL/hour maintenance reference and repeated checks of ABCs, observations, injury sites, IV site, tubing, bag, rate and infused volume. That reference is not a universal adult, child, heart-failure or renal-failure rate. Confirm the actual ordered plan and repeat assessment sooner if the patient, site or flow changes rather than waiting for a scheduled interval.
同页给出约75毫升／小时的维持参考，并要求重复检查ABCs、观察值、伤处、静脉点、管路、液袋、流速及已入量。该参考不是成人、儿童、心衰或肾衰通用速度。应确认真实计划，患者、穿刺点或流速变化时提前复评，不能只等固定间隔。

00:39:45.864 --> 00:40:12.912
The page40 adult diagram links arrest recognition to CPR and early AED analysis. With basic bag-mask care it uses30compressions to2breaths; a shock-advised branch delivers the shock then resumes CPR, and the no-shock branch also resumes CPR before the next analysis cycle. No shock advised does not mean circulation is present. Organized electrical activity alone does not prove a pulse.
第40页成人图把骤停识别连到CPR与尽早AED分析。基础球囊面罩照护采用30次按压配2次通气；建议电击分支电击后恢复CPR，不建议电击分支也先恢复CPR再到下一分析周期。不建议电击不表示已有循环，有组织电活动也不能证明有脉搏。

00:40:12.912 --> 00:40:51.576
The school2025 page40 lists30minutes in its continuation box; pages42-45 also describe medical-oversight consultation and reversible-cause/transport decisions, including a20minute consultation point. The later public copy adds a30/40minute distinction and changes several consultation statements. These are materially different texts, not one blended timer. Current N02 directs resuscitation decision-making to its relevant pathway and clinical consultation; an elapsed time alone is not termination authority.
学校2025年第40页继续复苏框列30分钟；42至45页还讨论医疗监督咨询、可逆病因及转运，包括20分钟咨询点。较新公共副本增加30／40分钟区分并改变多处咨询条款。这些文字实质不同，不能混成一个计时器。现行N02把复苏决策交给相关流程及临床咨询，经过某段时间本身不授权终止。

00:40:51.576 --> 00:41:27.384
Pages42-43 emphasize rate100-120/minute, full recoil, minimal interruption, early defibrillation and compressor rotation when possible. The adult reference is5-6cm; the school also prints a broad one-third-to-one-half size adjustment that must not become a universal adult depth rule. The selected current pediatric comparison uses at least one-third chest depth, approximately4cm for infants and5cm for children, rather than deliberately targeting one-half.
第42至43页强调每分钟100至120次、完全回弹、尽量少中断、尽早除颤及条件允许时轮换。成人参考深度为5至6厘米；学校还印有宽泛的胸径三分之一至二分之一体型调整，不能变成通用成人深度规则。所选现行儿科比较为至少胸径三分之一，婴儿约4厘米、儿童约5厘米，而非故意以二分之一为目标。

00:41:27.384 --> 00:42:04.152
The page41 infant/child diagram uses30:2 for one rescuer and15:2 for two; it also places neonatal3:1 in the same diagram. Page44 separately says no AED for a neonate. Do not follow the shared graphic’s shock loop as a neonatal AED instruction or apply birth-transition3:1 to every later infant collapse. First identify the age, circumstances and correct resuscitation framework; pediatric BLS and resuscitation at birth are not the same algorithm.
第41页婴儿儿童图采用单人30比2、双人15比2，但同图还放入新生儿3比1；第44页另写新生儿不用AED。不能把共用图的电击循环当新生儿AED指示，也不能把出生过渡期3比1用于之后每次婴儿倒地。先识别年龄、情境及正确复苏框架；儿科BLS与出生时复苏不是同一算法。

00:42:04.152 --> 00:42:42.264
Page44’s2025 newborn sequence starts with an under100 description but uses under60 to move through its early ventilation steps; the2026 comparison changes those early gates to under100, including a later transition. Neither old staircase should replace the current neonatal algorithm. In the current framework, apnea/gasping or heart rate below100 requires positive-pressure ventilation; compressions are considered for persistent rate below60 after effective ventilation and correction, not simply for every rate below100.
2025年第44页新生儿顺序开头描述低于100，却在早期通气步骤转移处用低于60；2026年比较本把早期门槛改成低于100，后续转移也有改变。两种旧阶梯都不能代替现行新生儿算法。现行框架中，无呼吸、喘息或心率低于100需要正压通气；有效通气及纠正后持续低于60才考虑按压，并非所有低于100都按压。

00:42:42.264 --> 00:43:18.096
Page46 distinguishes an effective cough from severe obstruction and then loss of responsiveness. The selected AHA2025 comparison uses five back blows then five abdominal thrusts for responsive adults/children with severe obstruction; infants receive back blows and chest thrusts, not abdominal thrusts. If unresponsive, start CPR with compressions and remove only a visible object when opening the airway. Do not use the school’s initial failed-breath wording to delay that response, and never perform blind finger sweeps.
第46页区分有效咳嗽、严重梗阻及反应丧失。所选AHA2025比较对有反应成人儿童严重梗阻采用5次背击再5次腹冲；婴儿用背击及胸冲，不做腹冲。失去反应后从按压开始CPR，开放气道时只取可见异物。不能因学校起始试气失败的措辞而延误此反应，也不做盲目手指探扫。

00:43:18.096 --> 00:43:55.560
Page50’s fixed-flow/COPD and blanket high-flow statements differ from current assessment-led oxygen guidance. Current A07 gives a general94% target and a chronic-hypoxemia intervention band of88-90%, while the complaint-specific B05 text uses88-92%. Keep the named source and patient context visible rather than average these bands. Critical illness and unreliable oximetry require active support; do not withhold needed oxygen to obtain an untreated number.
第50页固定流量、COPD及笼统高流量表述，与现行评估主导氧疗不同。现行A07给出一般94%目标及慢性低氧干预88至90%区间，主诉特异B05正文则用88至92%。应保留具名来源及患者背景，不把区间取平均。危重及不可靠血氧测量需要积极支持，不能为取得未治疗数字而扣住必要氧气。

00:43:55.560 --> 00:44:29.664
That page’s statement that every adult mask below6L/min delivers less oxygen than room air is not a reliable universal device rule. Low flow in a simple mask can allow exhaled gas rebreathing, and reservoir/device performance matters. Flow in litres/minute, delivered oxygen fraction and airway pressure are different quantities. Choose the actual device instructions and current pathway; more flow does not correct an obstructed airway or absent ventilation by itself.
该页声称成人面罩低于每分钟6升就一定比空气含氧少，不是可靠通用装置规则。简单面罩流量过低可允许呼出气再吸入，储氧囊及装置性能也重要。升／分钟流量、实际吸氧浓度及气道压力是不同量。应依真实装置说明及现行流程选择；流量更大本身不能纠正气道阻塞或无通气。

00:44:29.664 --> 00:44:59.448
Pages51-52 describe CPAP as continuous pressure during spontaneous breathing, supporting recruitment and reducing work of breathing in selected patients. It does not deliver assisted breaths for a patient whose effort is failing. Positive intrathoracic pressure can also reduce venous return and blood pressure. Reassess breathing, alertness, mask tolerance, oxygenation and perfusion, not only the saturation display.
第51至52页把CPAP描述为自主呼吸中持续正压，在合适患者支持肺泡复张并减呼吸功；它不为努力衰竭的患者送辅助呼吸。胸内正压也可减少静脉回流及血压。应复评呼吸、清醒度、面罩耐受、氧合及灌注，不只看血氧显示。

00:44:59.448 --> 00:45:41.400
The school CPAP page requires age13orabove, wakefulness/commands, an open airway and its listed distress criteria, including rate above24, saturation below94% on oxygen and accessory-muscle use. It excludes impaired airway protection, hypoventilation/arrest, aspiration risk, poor mask fit, traumatic respiratory distress, tracheostomy, suspected pneumothorax and systolic pressure below90. Current PR09 also specifies the relevant CPAP training and recommends PCP consultation. Reading the table does not replace either requirement.
学校CPAP页要求13岁及以上、清醒遵指令、气道开放及所列窘迫条件，包括频率高于24、给氧后血氧低于94%及辅助肌使用；排除气道保护差、低通气或停呼吸、误吸风险、面罩不合、创伤性窘迫、气切、疑气胸及收缩压低于90。现行PR09还规定相关CPAP培训，并建议PCP咨询。读表不能代替这两项要求。

00:45:41.400 --> 00:46:10.320
Page52 limits CPAP and PEEP escalation to10cmH2O, while page53’s device chart also displays higher columns. A displayed column is not permission to exceed the procedure cap. Nor does a litre/minute flow number equal a centimetre-of-water pressure. Current PR09 follows the manufacturer flow chart and its own escalation limit; no unverified chart for a different device is substituted.
第52页把CPAP与PEEP升级限制为10厘米水柱，但第53页装置表也显示更高列。显示一列并不授权超过操作上限。升／分钟的流量数字也不等于厘米水柱压力。现行PR09使用制造商流量表及其自身升级限制，不能替换成另一装置的未核实表。

00:46:10.320 --> 00:46:47.664
The school page55 lists prior allergy history among its criteria; the later public copy removes it. Do not wait for a known prior allergy, rash or profound hypotension before recognizing a compatible systemic reaction. Current E09 prioritizes intramuscular epinephrine and ABC support; salbutamol is an adjunct after epinephrine, and antihistamines do not replace it. The school lists diphenhydramine under PCP, whereas current E09 places it under ACP; the exam page does not expand current authority.
学校第55页把既往过敏史列为条件，较新公共本删掉该项。不能等已知过敏史、皮疹或严重低压才识别相符全身反应。现行E09优先肌注肾上腺素及ABC支持，沙丁胺醇为之后辅助，抗组胺不能替代。学校把苯海拉明列在PCP下，现行E09则放ACP下；考试页不扩展当前权限。

00:46:47.664 --> 00:47:26.760
Page56 emphasizes reduced responsiveness with slow, limited-volume breathing. Support airway and effective ventilation, obtain exposure history and glucose, and use the current opioid pathway rather than waiting for naloxone to work. Its glucose cross-reference uses less-than-or-equal4mmol/L, whereas page57 and current E01 define the correction gate as below4. Keep the exact inequality difference visible; measurement quality, symptoms and the active pathway determine the response, not an invented compromise cutoff.
第56页强调反应下降及频率慢、潮气量小的呼吸。应支持气道和有效通气、获取接触史及血糖，并用现行阿片流程，不能等纳洛酮起效。其血糖交叉条目用小于等于4mmol/L，而第57页及现行E01纠正门槛为低于4。应明示不等号差异；反应取决于测量质量、症状及现行流程，不是自创折中界值。

00:47:26.760 --> 00:48:02.904
BVM with PEEP adds end-expiratory pressure to assisted breaths and depends on an effective closed mask seal. It is not CPAP delivered to an apneic patient. Current general PR10 excludes adult systolic pressure at or below90, cardiac arrest, suspected pneumothorax and traumatic respiratory arrest, with age-specific pediatric pressure limits; neonatal specialty instructions are a separate context. Do not turn the school’s8-10/minute PEEP paragraph into a rate for every child, newborn or resuscitation.
球囊面罩加PEEP在辅助通气后保留呼气末压力，依赖有效封闭面罩密合，不是给无呼吸患者做CPAP。现行一般PR10排除成人收缩压小于等于90、心脏骤停、疑气胸及创伤性呼吸骤停，并有年龄特异儿科血压限制；新生儿专门指示属于另一背景。不能把学校PEEP段每分钟8至10次用成所有儿童、新生儿或复苏的频率。

00:48:02.904 --> 00:48:45.240
Page57 includes unexplained altered consciousness even without known diabetes. Check airway/breathing, glucose and stroke features, then select a permitted route using airway protection and access. Its exam-copy PCP box lists D10W10-25g as100-250mL of10% solution and glucagon when IV access is unavailable; verify the current monograph rather than treating that box as an independent prescription. An oral product is not safe merely because it can enter the mouth. Recheck glucose and mentation and investigate persistent illness.
第57页也包括没有已知糖尿病的原因不明意识改变。应检查气道呼吸、血糖及卒中特征，再依据气道保护及通路选择获准途径。其考试副本PCP框列D10W10至25克，即10%溶液100至250毫升，以及无IV通路时胰高血糖素；须核实现行专论，不能把该框当独立处方。口服产品能进嘴，不等于安全。应复查血糖与意识，继续调查持续疾病。

00:48:45.240 --> 00:49:13.872
Original retrieval: a dyspneic patient initially follows commands on CPAP but becomes drowsy with weaker, shallower breaths and worsening perfusion. State the changed findings, recognize that the original CPAP assumptions no longer hold, and move to the appropriate supported-airway/ventilation plan with help. Turning up pressure to reach a saturation number does not fix lost respiratory effort or airway protection.
原创回忆练习：气促患者起初用CPAP时可遵指令，随后嗜睡、呼吸更弱更浅、灌注恶化。应说清变化，识别原CPAP前提已不成立，并在求助下转入合适气道与通气支持计划。为追血氧数而调高压力，不能修复呼吸努力或气道保护丧失。

00:49:13.872 --> 00:49:25.992
Use this retrieval sequence after each guide. The purpose is not to memorize a diagnosis label; it is to show how the reading informs one defensible decision and what you would reassess.
每份指南后都使用这套回忆顺序。目标不是记住诊断标签，而是说明阅读内容如何支持一项有依据的决策，以及你将复查什么。

00:49:25.992 --> 00:49:40.008
A strong answer identifies a finding, explains why it matters, names uncertainty and stays at the right provider level. If the source edition or page is not verified, say so instead of guessing.
好的答案会指出一项发现、解释其意义、说明不确定性，并遵守正确执业层级。若教材版本或页码尚未核实，应如实说明，不要猜测。
